{%- comment -%}
  The "inc. tax" note that follows a price.

  **One switch, and it is `settings.show_tax_note`** (Theme settings →
  Pricing). Every surface that shows a price obeys it and none can override it,
  so "is it on?" has exactly one answer.

  Most Loved, the Lookbook and the bag drawer each carried a second toggle of
  their own, ANDed with this one. They were removed on request: a note that
  qualifies a price is a statement about how the shop prices, not a per-row
  style choice, and three extra switches made the shop-wide one hard to trust.

  The wording lives in `locales/en.default.json`, so it translates. It is not a
  theme setting: changing "inc. all taxes and fees" to "inkl. MwSt." is a
  localisation, not a per-shop style choice.

  There are two wordings, on request. Everywhere a price has room to be
  qualified in full it reads `products.tax_note` — "inc. all taxes and fees".
  The **product card** takes `short: true` and reads `products.tax_note_short`
  — "inc. all taxes" — because a card's price line is a single row beside the
  figure at 15px, and the longer sentence wraps it onto two.

  Accepts:
    short - true for the card's shorter wording. Omit everywhere else.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign show = settings.show_tax_note

  assign note_key = 'products.tax_note'
  if short
    assign note_key = 'products.tax_note_short'
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The leading space is real, not decoration. Callers trim around the render, so
  without it the markup is `$19.99<small>inc. all taxes</small>` — spaced by the
  margin on screen, but run together as one word when read aloud or copied.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if show -%}
  {{- ' ' -}}<small class="price-tax">{{ note_key | t }}</small>
{%- endif -%}
